COMPLETE PIPELINE EXECUTION STEPS (END-TO-END)
From ZERO → PR → Auto Slack → Merge → Cloud Build → Cloud Run → Slack Success/Failure
 PHASE 1 — GitHub Setup (One-Time Only)
 Create a Service Account in GCP

Go to GCP → IAM → Service Accounts → Create:

Name: github-actions-sa

Roles (assign all below):

Cloud Build Editor
Artifact Registry Writer
Cloud Run Admin
Storage Admin
Service Account User
IAM Service Account Token Creator

 Create JSON Key for the SA

Service Account → Keys → Create Key → JSON

Download file → open it → copy contents.

 Add Secrets in GitHub Repository

Go to:
 GitHub Repo → Settings → Secrets & Variables → Actions

Add the following:

Secret Name	Value
GCP_SA_KEY	Entire JSON key
SLACK_WEBHOOK_URL	Slack webhook URL
Install Google Cloud SDK GitHub Actions

(No manual work. The YAML uses it.)

 PHASE 2 — Slack Setup
 Create Slack Incoming Webhook

Slack → Apps → Incoming Webhooks

Steps:

Choose Slack channel → Add Webhook

Copy Webhook URL

Save it to GitHub secret: SLACK_WEBHOOK_URL

 PHASE 3 — Create the GitHub Workflow YAML

Go to repo:

repo/.github/workflows/day38-full-pipeline.yml


Paste the final YAML (we already built this).

Commit it to day38-pr-test.

 PHASE 4 — Branching & PR Flow
 Create a feature branch
git checkout -b day38-pr-test


Make some changes → commit → push.

 Create a Pull Request

From GitHub UI:
PR: day38-pr-test → main

 When PR is created:

GitHub workflow triggers

Slack gets:

PR Triggered!

 PHASE 5 — PR Review Workflow

Nothing to do.

PR builds (if any future validation added)

Slack is notified

You review PR manually

 PHASE 6 — Merge PR to Main
 Click “Merge PR”

Once PR is approved → Merge.

 This triggers the deploy_after_merge job.

 PHASE 7 — Deployment Pipeline Steps

When PR merges → GitHub Actions triggers:

 Build Docker Image Using Cloud Build

Command executed:

gcloud builds submit . --tag gcr.io/project-id/day38-image:latest --async


Because it's --async, Cloud Build logs do not break the pipeline.

Extractor finds:

Build ID

Build Logs URL

 Deploy to Cloud Run

Command:

gcloud run deploy day38-service --image gcr.io/... --region us-central1


Cloud Run deploys your service & assigns a URL:

Example:

https://day38-service-541531337654.us-central1.run.app

 PHASE 8 — Slack Notifications
Slack — Deployment Success Message

Sent with:

Commit SHA

Cloud Build Logs URL

Cloud Run Service URL

Example:

 Deployment Successful!
 Service: https://day38-service...
 Commit: 3e423bc
 Build Logs: https://console.cloud.google.com/cloud-build/builds/...

Slack — Deployment Failed Message

If ANY step fails, Slack gets failure alert:

Deployment FAILED!
 Commit: 3e423bc
 Build Logs: https://console.cloud.google.com/cloud-build/builds/...

 PHASE 9 — Validate Deployment
Test URL

Open the Cloud Run URL from Slack:

https://day38-service-xxxxxx.us-central1.run.app


You should see your Day38 application.
